\subsection{Overhead model}
Aggregating across the five quantized modules, total INT4 MACs were 26,697,728. Histogram updates totaled 320 increments (approximately 64 per module), and metadata summed to 75 bits per batch (approximately 15 bits per module). The modeled relative overhead, defined as histogram operations plus header bits divided by MACs, was 1.48e-5, effectively zero compared to compute. Figure~\ref{fig:latency} shows similar wall-clock times across methods, and Figure~\ref{fig:metadata} illustrates the metadata amortization property of a single 15-bit header per layer per batch.

